  "reason": "The best result so far is config_002 (RNA-only, multi-profile, PCA n2000, avgpool) at 0.591 accuracy, and multi-profile + avgpool is clearly the strongest aggregation strategy (0.591 vs 0.519 for transformer). The key unexplored dimension is the RNA encoder: PCA is a linear method, while scvi_n200 is a learned non-linear encoder that may capture richer single-cell structure. Config_005 (scvi_n200, multi-profile, avgpool) isolates the encoder effect by changing only the RNA encoder relative to config_002, making it a clean A/B comparison. Since image-only performance is very weak (0.208), improving the RNA signal is the most direct path to higher accuracy. With 5 experiments remaining, establishing whether a learned encoder beats PCA in the best-known setting is the highest-value uncertainty to resolve before investing in multimodal fusion experiments."
